        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> That's good if you're using lots of mini.nvim plugins but if you're using one it would be good if each project had its own changelog. If it is automated later it could be possible.\n\nAh, you mean changelog in each standalone repo? It is straightforward to implement only if changelog files are initially split in separate files (like README files). However, I would like to have a single top-level changelog file for 'mini.nvim' and duplicating information in several files is not a good idea.\n\nSo as extracting changelog for a specific module-version combo is fairly convoluted, I don't think releases in standalone repos will get their custom changelogs. This is aligned with the overall structure of 'mini.nvim' project: the library is main priority while standalone repos are synchronized with it.\n\nAlso, as releases are not so common and are done in sync for 'mini.nvim' and all standalone repos, going to [global changelog](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md) should not be hugely inconvenient.",
            "created_at": "2025-04-27T19:12:37Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1759#issuecomment-2833599671",
